# Game bundles under games-src/ must checkout byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this rule, git (with core.autocrlf=true on Windows) converts LF line
# endings to CRLF at checkout, so the same text files measure bigger on Windows
# than on Linux CI. That made the bundleBytes content check fail on CI even
# though it passed locally. `-text` disables line-ending conversion for every
# file under games-src/, so all platforms see the exact same bytes.
#
# The playable bundles themselves are copied into public/play/ by
# scripts/sync-local-games.mjs, which copies bytes as-is, so this rule has no
# effect on the deployed site.
games-src/** -text
